WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.549
Previously on Supernatural 22 years ago

00:00:07.584 --> 00:00:08.667
Sammy.

00:00:09.191 --> 00:00:11.081
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:11.116 --> 00:00:11.990
Go!

00:00:12.025 --> 00:00:14.544
Their mother Mysteriously died

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:16.982
Now two brothers...
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.267
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:19.302 --> 00:00:21.518
Are on a quest to find their father

00:00:22.464 --> 00:00:23.498
This is dad's book.

00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:25.711
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:25.746 --> 00:00:27.762
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:29.490
The family business.

00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:30.898
I got to find dad.

00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:33.472
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:52.222 --> 00:00:55.288
Where have you got those amp
up to? A hundred thousand volts.

00:00:55.438 --> 00:00:58.091
Damn. Yeah, I want this raw
head extra freaking crispy.

00:00:58.126 --> 00:01:00.745
Now, remember you only get
one shot with these things.

00:01:01.226 --> 00:01:03.188
So make it count.

00:01:35.989 --> 00:01:37.014
On three.

00:01:37.887 --> 00:01:38.955
One.

00:01:39.444 --> 00:01:40.762
Two.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.474
Three.

00:01:46.151 --> 00:01:47.738
Is it still here?

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:48.888
Okay.

00:01:48.923 --> 00:01:50.803
Okay, hold your sister's hand.
We're gonna get you out of here.

00:01:50.838 --> 00:01:52.470
Let's go, let's go.

00:01:55.938 --> 00:01:57.491
All right, go!

00:02:00.231 --> 00:02:01.683
Sam!

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.480
Sam, get them out of here!

00:02:09.515 --> 00:02:10.860
Here, take this!

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.235
Run!

00:02:22.255 --> 00:02:24.663
Come on!

00:03:02.972 --> 00:03:04.491
Dean!

00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:06.147
Dean!

00:03:06.368 --> 00:03:07.256
Hey!

00:03:07.693 --> 00:03:09.599
Hey, hey!

00:03:19.211 --> 00:03:20.742
Sorry, I'm so sorry to ask.

00:03:20.777 --> 00:03:23.115
There doesn't seem to
be any insurance on file.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.157
Right, um...

00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:28.405
Okay.

00:03:29.865 --> 00:03:33.176
Okay, Mr. Burkevits.

00:03:35.649 --> 00:03:39.279
Look, we can finish this
up later. No, no it's okay.

00:03:39.314 --> 00:03:42.286
We were just taking a short cut
through the neighborhood and um...

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:45.073
Windows were all down,
we heard some screaming.

00:03:45.108 --> 00:03:47.826
We drove pass the house
and we stopped, ran in.

00:03:47.861 --> 00:03:49.356
And you found the kids in the basement.

00:03:49.391 --> 00:03:50.227
Yeah.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.508
Well, thank god you did.

00:03:52.917 --> 00:03:56.045
Excuse me. Sure, thanks for your help.

00:03:56.311 --> 00:03:57.256
Hey, doc. Is he...

00:03:57.291 --> 00:03:59.428
He's resting. And?

00:03:59.463 --> 00:04:01.953
The electrocution
triggered a heart attack.

00:04:01.988 --> 00:04:06.709
A pretty massive one. I'm
afraid his heart, it's damaged.

00:04:06.744 --> 00:04:09.386
How damaged? We've done all we can.

00:04:09.421 --> 00:04:12.643
We can try and keep him
comfortable at this point but...

00:04:12.678 --> 00:04:15.866
I'll give him a couple of
weeks at most, maybe a month.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.397
No, no, there is...

00:04:17.432 --> 00:04:20.278
There's gotta be something you
can do. Some kind of treatment.

00:04:20.313 --> 00:04:22.522
We can't work miracles.

00:04:22.557 --> 00:04:25.200
I really am sorry.

00:04:34.489 --> 00:04:40.107
You ever actually watched
daytime TV? It's terrible.

00:04:41.757 --> 00:04:43.342
I talked to your doctor.

00:04:43.377 --> 00:04:45.790
That fabric soft teddy bear, oh.

00:04:45.825 --> 00:04:48.699
I'll hunt that bitch down. Dean...

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.947
Yeah.

00:04:50.982 --> 00:04:54.743
All right, well. Looks like
you're gonna leave town without me.

00:04:54.778 --> 00:04:56.808
What are you talking about?
I'm not gonna leave you here.

00:04:56.843 --> 00:04:58.713
Hey, if you take care of that car.

00:04:58.748 --> 00:05:00.549
I'll swear I'll hunt your ass.

00:05:00.584 --> 00:05:04.551
I don't think that's funny. Uh,
come on. It's a little funny.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.528
Look, Sam. What can I say,
man. It's a dangerous gig.

00:05:14.563 --> 00:05:16.976
I drew the short straw.
That it, end of story.

00:05:17.011 --> 00:05:19.254
Don't talk like that, all right?

00:05:19.289 --> 00:05:22.256
We still have options. What options?

00:05:22.291 --> 00:05:25.154
Get burial or cremation?

00:05:25.189 --> 00:05:28.017
I know it's not easy.

00:05:29.165 --> 00:05:31.788
But I'm gonna die.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.702
And you can't stop it.

00:05:36.695 --> 00:05:38.436
Watch me.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.935
This is John Winchester.
I can't be reached.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:43.399
If this is an emergency
call my son Dean.

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:48.702
866-907-3235.
He can help.

00:05:48.737 --> 00:05:51.474
Hey, dad. It's Sam.

00:05:52.745 --> 00:05:55.111
You probably won't get this but uh...

00:05:55.146 --> 00:05:57.064
It's Dean...

00:05:57.099 --> 00:05:59.803
He's sick and uh...

00:05:59.967 --> 00:06:03.588
Doctors says there
nothing they can do. Um...

00:06:04.874 --> 00:06:06.260
But uh...

00:06:06.295 --> 00:06:09.278
They don't know things
we know, right? Um...

00:06:09.313 --> 00:06:11.942
So, don't worry, cause I'm uh...

00:06:11.977 --> 00:06:15.066
Gonna do everything it
takes to get him better.

00:06:15.982 --> 00:06:17.460
All right.

00:06:17.495 --> 00:06:19.868
Just wanted you to know.

00:06:34.482 --> 00:06:35.811
What the hell are you doing here?

00:06:35.846 --> 00:06:38.818
I checked myself out. Are you crazy?

00:06:38.853 --> 00:06:42.896
I'm not gonna die in a hospital
where the nurses aren't even hot.

00:06:43.139 --> 00:06:45.407
You know, this whole...

00:06:45.442 --> 00:06:47.874
I laugh in the face of
death thing... It's crap.

00:06:47.909 --> 00:06:50.199
I can see right through it.

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.158
Yeah, whatever dude.

00:06:52.193 --> 00:06:54.389
Have you even slept?
You look worse than me.

00:06:54.424 --> 00:06:58.160
I've been scattering the
internet for the last three days.

00:06:59.737 --> 00:07:02.780
Calling every contact
in dad journal. For what?

00:07:02.815 --> 00:07:04.608
For what'll help you.

00:07:04.643 --> 00:07:07.699
One of dad's friends
Joshua. He called me back.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:10.271
Told me about a guy in
Nebraska. Specialist.

00:07:10.306 --> 00:07:12.808
You're not gonna let me
die in peace, are you?

00:07:12.843 --> 00:07:14.861
I'm not gonna let you die, period.

00:07:14.896 --> 00:07:17.380
We're going.

00:07:37.525 --> 00:07:40.642
The church of Roy Le Grange
Faith Healer. Witness the miracle

00:07:41.945 --> 00:07:44.899
I got you. I got it!

00:07:45.824 --> 00:07:47.756
Man, you're a lying bastard.

00:07:47.791 --> 00:07:49.855
I thought you said we
were going to see a doctor.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.578
I believe I said a 'specialist'.

00:07:51.613 --> 00:07:53.852
Look Dean, this guy's
suppose to be the real deal.

00:07:53.887 --> 00:07:57.322
I can't believe you brought me here to see
some guy who heals people out of a tent!

00:07:57.357 --> 00:08:00.336
Reverend Le Grange is a
great man. Yeah, that's nice.

00:08:00.371 --> 00:08:02.591
I have a right to protest.
This man is a fraud.

00:08:02.626 --> 00:08:05.074
He's bilking all these people
out of their hard earned money!

00:08:05.109 --> 00:08:08.513
This is a place of
worship. Let's go, move it.

00:08:08.548 --> 00:08:10.755
I take it he's not part of the flock.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.176
What would people see something
that they can't explain.

00:08:13.211 --> 00:08:15.563
There's controversy. Come
on, Sam. A Faith Healer?

00:08:15.598 --> 00:08:18.913
Maybe it's time to have
a little faith Dean.

00:08:19.666 --> 00:08:21.733
You know what I got faith in? Reality.

00:08:21.768 --> 00:08:23.966
Knowing what's really going on.

00:08:24.001 --> 00:08:25.548
How can you be a skeptic?

00:08:25.583 --> 00:08:27.010
With the things we see everyday.

00:08:27.045 --> 00:08:29.021
Exactly, we see them.
We know they're real.

00:08:29.056 --> 00:08:30.319
But if you know evil's out there

00:08:30.354 --> 00:08:31.920
How can you not believe
good's out there too?

00:08:31.955 --> 00:08:33.486
Cause I've seen what
evil does to good people.

00:08:33.521 --> 00:08:36.307
Maybe god works in mysterious ways.

00:08:36.868 --> 00:08:38.950
Maybe he does.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:41.265
I think you just turned
me Around on the subject.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.349
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:08:43.384 --> 00:08:45.477
I'm Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:45.512 --> 00:08:47.249
Leila.

00:08:47.284 --> 00:08:50.645
Sir, if you're not a believer
then why are you here?

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:54.156
Well, apparently my brother here
believes enough for the both of us.

00:08:54.191 --> 00:08:57.446
Come on Leila. It's
about to start. All right.

00:08:57.481 --> 00:08:59.216
Bye.

00:08:59.483 --> 00:09:02.433
Well, I bet you, she can
work in mysterious ways.

00:09:02.468 --> 00:09:04.561
Ladies and gentlemen, please be seated.

00:09:04.596 --> 00:09:07.889
We're starting in just a moment.
Welcome all faiths True believers revival

00:09:10.204 --> 00:09:13.506
Yeah, peace love and trust all over.

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:19.222
Come on.

00:09:19.257 --> 00:09:20.561
Don't, we're sitting here.

00:09:20.596 --> 00:09:21.998
We're sitting up front.

00:09:22.033 --> 00:09:23.400
What? Why? Come on.

00:09:23.435 --> 00:09:24.927
Oh, come on Sam.

00:09:24.962 --> 00:09:26.384
You're all right?

00:09:26.419 --> 00:09:30.086
This is ridiculous. I'm
good, dude. Get off me.

00:09:31.113 --> 00:09:33.096
Perfect. Yeah, perfect.

00:09:33.131 --> 00:09:35.064
Take it off

00:09:44.786 --> 00:09:49.388
Each morning my wife Sue
Ann brings me the news.

00:09:49.423 --> 00:09:51.939
Never seems good, does it? No.

00:09:51.974 --> 00:09:54.421
Seems like there's always someone

00:09:54.456 --> 00:09:59.863
Committing some immoral,
unspeakable act. That's right.

00:09:59.898 --> 00:10:02.989
But I say to you. God is watching.

00:10:03.024 --> 00:10:04.434
Here, here.

00:10:04.469 --> 00:10:10.987
God rewards the good and he
punishes the corrupt. Right.

00:10:11.022 --> 00:10:15.614
It is the Lord who does
the healing here friends.

00:10:15.649 --> 00:10:20.172
The Lord who guides me
and chosen who to heal

00:10:20.207 --> 00:10:23.788
By helping me to see into
people's hearts. Amen.

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:26.233
Yeah, rid of their wallets.

00:10:26.268 --> 00:10:28.643
You think so young man?

00:10:30.084 --> 00:10:33.503
Sorry. No, no. Don't be.

00:10:33.538 --> 00:10:38.479
Just watch what you say around a
blind man. We got real sharp ears.

00:10:39.535 --> 00:10:41.929
What's your name son?

00:10:42.567 --> 00:10:45.342
Dean. Dean.

00:10:47.083 --> 00:10:50.871
I want you to come up here with me.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:00.402
No, it's okay.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.690
What are you doing?

00:11:01.725 --> 00:11:05.618
You come here to be healed, haven't you?

00:11:07.829 --> 00:11:10.647
Oh, yeah but uh...

00:11:10.682 --> 00:11:14.623
Maybe you should just pick someone else.

00:11:17.123 --> 00:11:21.743
I didn't pick you Dean. The Lord did.

00:11:23.224 --> 00:11:25.622
Get up there!

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:29.994
Yes. Yes. Amen.

00:11:36.236 --> 00:11:37.962
You're ready?

00:11:37.997 --> 00:11:40.800
Yeah, with no disrespect but uh...

00:11:40.835 --> 00:11:43.623
I'm not exactly a believer.

00:11:43.768 --> 00:11:45.653
You will be son.

00:11:45.688 --> 00:11:47.538
You will be.

00:11:47.722 --> 00:11:50.396
Pray with me friends.

00:12:14.068 --> 00:12:18.260
All right now.

00:12:27.258 --> 00:12:29.862
All right now.

00:12:34.311 --> 00:12:36.028
Dean!

00:12:40.885 --> 00:12:42.925
Say something!

00:12:56.256 --> 00:12:58.111
So you really feel okay?

00:12:58.146 --> 00:12:59.464
I feel fine Sam.

00:12:59.499 --> 00:13:03.361
Well, according to all your tests.
There's nothing wrong with your heart.

00:13:03.396 --> 00:13:05.121
No sign there ever was.

00:13:05.156 --> 00:13:08.888
Not that a man your age should
be having heart trouble but uh...

00:13:08.923 --> 00:13:10.902
Still it's strange, it does happen.

00:13:10.937 --> 00:13:12.063
What do you mean strange?

00:13:12.098 --> 00:13:15.711
Well, just yesterday a young
guy like you. 27, athletic.

00:13:15.746 --> 00:13:18.414
I don't know a heart attack.

00:13:19.255 --> 00:13:21.053
Thanks doc.

00:13:21.088 --> 00:13:22.851
No problem.

00:13:24.006 --> 00:13:26.112
That's odd. Maybe it's coincidence.

00:13:26.147 --> 00:13:28.267
People's heart give up all
the time, man. No they don't.

00:13:28.302 --> 00:13:30.352
Look Dean. Do we really have
to look this one in the mouth?

00:13:30.387 --> 00:13:33.021
Why can't we just be thankful that
the guy saved your life and move on?

00:13:33.056 --> 00:13:35.787
Because I can't shake
this feeling, that's why.

00:13:35.822 --> 00:13:37.739
What feeling?

00:13:37.774 --> 00:13:41.204
When I was healed. I just, I felt wrong.

00:13:41.239 --> 00:13:44.510
Felt cold and for a second

00:13:44.545 --> 00:13:46.429
I saw someone. I saw this old man.

00:13:46.464 --> 00:13:48.278
I'm telling you Sam. It was a spirit.

00:13:48.313 --> 00:13:50.922
But if there was something there
Dean. I think I would have seen it too.

00:13:50.957 --> 00:13:53.150
I mean I've been seeing
awful lot of things lately.

00:13:53.185 --> 00:13:54.899
Well, excuse me psychic wonder.

00:13:54.934 --> 00:13:57.865
But you just need a
little faith on this one.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:02.042
Sam, I've been hunting long enough
to trust a feeling like this.

00:14:04.347 --> 00:14:06.334
Yeah, right.

00:14:07.406 --> 00:14:09.649
So what do you want to do?

00:14:09.684 --> 00:14:11.061
Why don't you to check
out that heart attack guy.

00:14:11.096 --> 00:14:13.292
I'm gonna visit the reverend.

00:14:16.221 --> 00:14:17.814
I feel great.

00:14:17.849 --> 00:14:19.372
Just trying to...

00:14:19.407 --> 00:14:21.488
You know, make sense of what happened.

00:14:21.523 --> 00:14:24.415
A miracle's what happened.

00:14:24.794 --> 00:14:29.321
Miracles come so often around Roy.

00:14:30.014 --> 00:14:32.623
When did they start? The miracles.

00:14:32.658 --> 00:14:35.197
Woke up one morning stone blind.

00:14:35.232 --> 00:14:39.564
Doctors figured out I had cancer.
Told me I had maybe a month.

00:14:39.599 --> 00:14:41.157
So uh...

00:14:41.192 --> 00:14:43.448
We prayed for a miracle.

00:14:43.483 --> 00:14:46.063
I was weak but...

00:14:46.098 --> 00:14:49.492
I told Sue Ann to just keep on praying.

00:14:49.527 --> 00:14:51.064
I went into a coma.

00:14:51.099 --> 00:14:53.898
Doctors said I wouldn't
wake up but I did.

00:14:53.933 --> 00:14:56.398
And the cancer was gone.

00:14:56.433 --> 00:15:02.095
If it wasn't for these eyes, no
one would believe I ever had it.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.804
And suddenly you can heal people?

00:15:04.839 --> 00:15:07.412
I discovered it afterwards, yes.

00:15:07.447 --> 00:15:09.950
God's blessed me in many ways.

00:15:09.985 --> 00:15:15.520
And his flock swelled over night.
And this is just the beginning.

00:15:17.156 --> 00:15:19.372
Can I ask you one last question?

00:15:19.407 --> 00:15:21.641
Of course you can.

00:15:22.333 --> 00:15:24.893
Why? Why me?

00:15:24.928 --> 00:15:28.279
Out of all the sick people why save me?

00:15:28.314 --> 00:15:32.090
Well, like I said before.
The Lord guides me.

00:15:32.125 --> 00:15:39.541
I looked into your heart and you
just stood out from all the rest.

00:15:39.705 --> 00:15:43.332
What did you see in my heart?

00:15:43.367 --> 00:15:47.126
A young man with an important
purpose. A job to do.

00:15:47.161 --> 00:15:50.183
And it isn't finished.

00:15:51.908 --> 00:15:56.003
He seemed healthy. Swam
everyday. Didn't smoke.

00:15:56.038 --> 00:15:58.899
It's no so hard to act this
kind of scene. No bizarre.

00:15:58.934 --> 00:16:01.760
And you said he was running?
Right before he collapsed?

00:16:01.795 --> 00:16:03.672
Yeah, yeah. He was freaking out.

00:16:03.707 --> 00:16:05.418
Said that something was...

00:16:05.453 --> 00:16:07.095
After him. Did he say what?

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:10.783
Thin air, that's what. I
mean, there wasn't anything.

00:16:10.967 --> 00:16:12.854
All right, thanks.

00:16:15.309 --> 00:16:16.783
Hey buddy. You're...

00:16:16.818 --> 00:16:18.291
You're clock's busted.

00:16:18.326 --> 00:16:19.730
Oh, yeah. We uh...

00:16:19.765 --> 00:16:24.236
We can't get it working.
Just froze at 4:17.

00:16:24.271 --> 00:16:26.839
Is that the same time Marshall died?

00:16:26.874 --> 00:16:28.731
How did you know?

00:16:32.209 --> 00:16:34.756
Dean, hey. Hey.

00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:36.659
How you feeling? I feel good.

00:16:36.694 --> 00:16:39.091
Cured, I guess.

00:16:39.126 --> 00:16:40.689
What are you doing here?

00:16:40.724 --> 00:16:43.953
You know my mom. She wanted
to talk to the reverend.

00:16:43.988 --> 00:16:45.704
Leila.

00:16:46.738 --> 00:16:50.858
Yes, we're here again. Oh,
I'm sorry but Roy's resting.

00:16:50.893 --> 00:16:53.284
He won't be seeing anyone right now.

00:16:53.319 --> 00:16:55.320
Sue Ann please.

00:16:55.355 --> 00:16:57.998
This is our sixth time.
He's got to see us.

00:16:58.033 --> 00:17:00.213
Roy is aware of Leila's situation

00:17:00.248 --> 00:17:03.367
And he very well much wants to help
just as soon as the Lord allows.

00:17:03.402 --> 00:17:06.694
Have faith Mrs. Roke.

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.413
Why are you still even here?

00:17:16.448 --> 00:17:18.502
You've got what you wanted. Mom.

00:17:18.537 --> 00:17:20.365
Stop.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.976
No Leila this is too much.

00:17:23.011 --> 00:17:25.491
We've been to every single service.

00:17:25.526 --> 00:17:28.441
If Roy would stop choosing
these strangers over you.

00:17:28.476 --> 00:17:31.639
Strangers who don't even believe.

00:17:31.674 --> 00:17:34.802
I just can't pray any harder.

00:17:34.837 --> 00:17:37.448
Leila, what's wrong?

00:17:39.652 --> 00:17:41.944
I have this thing.

00:17:41.979 --> 00:17:44.236
It's a brain tumor.

00:17:44.691 --> 00:17:47.636
It's inoperable.

00:17:47.812 --> 00:17:51.547
In sixth months the doctors say...

00:17:55.982 --> 00:17:58.217
I'm sorry.

00:17:58.751 --> 00:18:00.651
It's okay.

00:18:00.686 --> 00:18:02.666
No.

00:18:02.952 --> 00:18:05.667
It isn't.

00:18:10.865 --> 00:18:15.278
Why do you deserve to
live more than my daughter?

00:18:43.652 --> 00:18:45.991
What did you find out?

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.631
I'm sorry.

00:18:48.819 --> 00:18:50.010
Sorry about what?

00:18:50.045 --> 00:18:55.579
Marshall Hall died at 4:17.

00:18:55.797 --> 00:18:58.285
The exact time I was healed. Yeah.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:01.863
So, I put together a list.
Everyone Roy's healed.

00:19:01.898 --> 00:19:05.509
Six people over the past year and I
cross checked them with local obits.

00:19:05.544 --> 00:19:08.245
Every time someone was
healed someone else died.

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:09.666
And each time the victim died

00:19:09.701 --> 00:19:12.572
Of the same symptom Le Grange
was healing at the time.

00:19:12.607 --> 00:19:15.443
Someone healed a cancer,
someone else died of cancer?

00:19:15.478 --> 00:19:18.849
Somehow. Le Grange...

00:19:19.033 --> 00:19:23.226
Is trading a life for another. Hello?

00:19:24.397 --> 00:19:26.101
Wait, wait, wait. So...

00:19:26.136 --> 00:19:28.713
Marshall Hall died to save me?

00:19:28.748 --> 00:19:30.642
Dean...

00:19:30.856 --> 00:19:33.282
The guy probably would have died anyway.

00:19:33.317 --> 00:19:35.708
And someone else would have been healed.

00:19:37.862 --> 00:19:40.230
You never should have brought me here.

00:19:40.265 --> 00:19:42.814
Dean, I was just trying
to save your life.

00:19:42.849 --> 00:19:45.363
But Sam, some guy is
dead now because of me!

00:19:45.398 --> 00:19:48.172
I didn't know.

00:19:49.008 --> 00:19:52.015
Pray with me friends.

00:19:52.857 --> 00:19:56.046
The thing I don't understand
is how is Roy doing it?

00:19:56.081 --> 00:19:58.892
How's he trading a life for a life?

00:19:58.927 --> 00:20:01.674
Oh, he's not doing it.

00:20:01.819 --> 00:20:03.949
Something else is doing it for him.

00:20:03.984 --> 00:20:08.268
What do you mean? The
old man I saw on stage.

00:20:08.658 --> 00:20:10.456
I didn't want to believe
it. But deep down, I knew it.

00:20:10.491 --> 00:20:12.549
You knew what? What
are you talking about?

00:20:12.584 --> 00:20:16.946
There's only one thing that can
give and take life like that.

00:20:16.981 --> 00:20:19.613
We're dealing with a reaper.

00:21:19.521 --> 00:21:21.282
You really think it's the 'Grim Reaper'?

00:21:21.317 --> 00:21:24.303
Like Angel of Death, the
Collector of Soul the whole deal?

00:21:24.338 --> 00:21:26.829
No, no, no. Not 'The
Reaper'. A 'Reaper'.

00:21:26.864 --> 00:21:29.180
There's reaper law in pretty
much every culture on earth.

00:21:29.215 --> 00:21:30.949
They go by a hundred different names.

00:21:30.984 --> 00:21:32.932
It's possible this one's one of them.

00:21:32.967 --> 00:21:34.845
But you said you saw a dude in a suit.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:38.845
What? You think he should be
working the whole black robe thing?

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.731
You said it yourself that
the clock stopped right?

00:21:42.635 --> 00:21:44.669
Reapers stop time.

00:21:44.704 --> 00:21:46.190
And you can only see them
when they're coming at you

00:21:46.225 --> 00:21:48.247
Which is why I could
see him and you couldn't.

00:21:48.282 --> 00:21:50.234
Maybe. There's nothing
else that could be Sam.

00:21:50.269 --> 00:21:53.499
The question is how's Roy
controlling the damn thing.

00:21:53.534 --> 00:21:55.190
That cross.

00:21:55.225 --> 00:21:57.624
What? There was this cross.

00:21:57.659 --> 00:22:02.236
I noticed it in the church
tent, I knew I seen it before.

00:22:07.961 --> 00:22:09.812
Here.

00:22:10.356 --> 00:22:11.461
Tarot?

00:22:11.496 --> 00:22:13.046
It makes sense.

00:22:13.081 --> 00:22:15.232
I mean, tarot dates back to
the early Christian, right?

00:22:15.267 --> 00:22:16.998
When some priests
were still using magic?

00:22:17.033 --> 00:22:18.694
And a few of them viewed
into the dark stuff.

00:22:18.729 --> 00:22:22.905
Necromancy and how to push
death away, how to cause it.

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:25.791
So Roy's using black
magic to bind the reaper.

00:22:25.826 --> 00:22:27.986
If he is, he's riding the whirlwind.

00:22:28.021 --> 00:22:31.942
It's like putting a dog
leash on a great white.

00:22:38.083 --> 00:22:40.826
Okay, then we stop Roy. How?

00:22:40.861 --> 00:22:41.831
You know how?

00:22:41.866 --> 00:22:43.265
Wait, what the hell are
you talking about Dean?

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:45.113
We can't kill Roy.

00:22:45.148 --> 00:22:46.301
Sam. The guy's playing god.

00:22:46.336 --> 00:22:48.953
He's deciding who lives and who
dies. That's a monster in my books.

00:22:48.988 --> 00:22:51.853
No, we're not gonna
kill a human being Dean.

00:22:51.888 --> 00:22:53.782
We do that, we're no better than he is.

00:22:53.817 --> 00:22:56.601
Okay, so we can't kill
Roy. We can't kill death.

00:22:56.636 --> 00:22:59.684
Any bright ideas college boy?

00:22:59.975 --> 00:23:01.306
Okay, uh...

00:23:01.341 --> 00:23:03.721
If Roy's using some kind
of black spell on the reaper

00:23:03.756 --> 00:23:06.149
We gotta figure out what it is.

00:23:06.184 --> 00:23:08.713
And how to break it.

00:23:13.799 --> 00:23:17.025
Service today.

00:23:21.777 --> 00:23:24.415
If Roy's using a spell.
There might be a spell book.

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:25.617
See if you can find it.

00:23:25.652 --> 00:23:28.481
Hurry up. Services start in 15
minutes. I'll try to stroll Roy.

00:23:28.516 --> 00:23:31.259
All right. Le Grange is
a fraud. He's no healer.

00:23:31.294 --> 00:23:32.961
Amen, brother. You
keep up the good work.

00:23:32.996 --> 00:23:34.650
Thank you.

00:24:31.478 --> 00:24:33.770
Encyclopedia of Christian
History Old & New Testament

00:25:00.334 --> 00:25:05.934
Openly gay teacher wins lawsuit
Strong message sent to Nations...

00:25:16.058 --> 00:25:19.316
Wright: 'local church a cult'

00:25:28.843 --> 00:25:29.726
What have you got?

00:25:29.761 --> 00:25:31.751
Roy's choosing victims
he sees as a immoral.

00:25:31.786 --> 00:25:33.706
And I think I know
who's next on his list.

00:25:33.741 --> 00:25:35.755
Remember the protestor?
The guy in the parking lot?

00:25:35.790 --> 00:25:37.814
Yeah. Yeah, I'll find him.

00:25:37.849 --> 00:25:40.795
But you can't let Roy
heal anyone, all right?

00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:02.346
Leila.

00:26:02.381 --> 00:26:05.606
Leila Roke, come up here child.

00:26:10.896 --> 00:26:12.898
Mom... Baby.

00:26:12.933 --> 00:26:14.900
I love you.

00:26:15.950 --> 00:26:18.042
Oh, man.

00:26:27.169 --> 00:26:29.846
Leila, listen to me.
You can't get up there.

00:26:29.881 --> 00:26:31.824
Why not? We've waited for months.

00:26:31.859 --> 00:26:33.623
You can't let Roy heal you.

00:26:33.658 --> 00:26:35.671
I don't understand. Roy
healed you, didn't he?

00:26:35.706 --> 00:26:37.649
I mean, why wouldn't
you at least let him try?

00:26:37.684 --> 00:26:40.890
Because if you do, something
bad is going to happen.

00:26:40.925 --> 00:26:44.096
I can't explain. I just need
you to believe me. Leila.

00:26:44.131 --> 00:26:46.295
Please...

00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:55.972
I'm sorry.

00:26:56.007 --> 00:26:57.875
Leila. Leila!

00:26:57.910 --> 00:26:59.743
Dear child.

00:27:00.834 --> 00:27:04.019
You deserve this. I knew
the Lord would reply me...

00:27:04.054 --> 00:27:06.952
I knew the Lord would reply me.

00:27:10.421 --> 00:27:12.286
Help!

00:27:19.366 --> 00:27:21.717
Pray with me friends.

00:27:25.804 --> 00:27:28.889
I hope you're ready. I am.

00:27:39.165 --> 00:27:40.506
Help!

00:27:40.541 --> 00:27:41.899
Help me please!

00:27:41.934 --> 00:27:43.257
Where is it?

00:27:43.472 --> 00:27:45.724
It's right there!

00:27:47.157 --> 00:27:49.169
Come on, come on.

00:27:57.920 --> 00:27:59.390
Fire!

00:27:59.425 --> 00:28:01.996
The tent's on fire!

00:28:02.144 --> 00:28:04.131
Fire! Everybody get out of here!

00:28:04.166 --> 00:28:06.716
Roy! Roy, please!

00:28:06.751 --> 00:28:08.864
Please don't stop. Please!

00:28:08.899 --> 00:28:10.840
Reverend, please!

00:28:10.875 --> 00:28:12.781
Please don't stop.

00:28:12.816 --> 00:28:14.400
Please.

00:28:14.435 --> 00:28:15.950
Friends.

00:28:15.985 --> 00:28:19.561
If you all just leave the tent
in an orderly fashion and...

00:28:19.596 --> 00:28:22.269
We'll figure out what's
going on out there and...

00:28:22.304 --> 00:28:25.161
I did it. I stopped Roy.

00:28:25.196 --> 00:28:28.018
David? I think its okay.

00:28:31.768 --> 00:28:33.378
No!

00:28:33.413 --> 00:28:34.605
Dean, it didn't work!

00:28:34.640 --> 00:28:36.626
The reaper's still coming!

00:28:37.600 --> 00:28:39.143
I'm telling you... I'm telling you.

00:28:39.178 --> 00:28:41.777
It must not have worked! Roy must
not be controlling this thing!

00:28:41.812 --> 00:28:44.305
Then who the hell is?

00:28:47.356 --> 00:28:49.469
Sue Ann.

00:29:03.611 --> 00:29:05.903
Help! Help me!

00:29:06.047 --> 00:29:07.837
Help!

00:29:22.268 --> 00:29:24.591
I got you. I got you.

00:29:27.134 --> 00:29:29.118
Thank god.

00:29:34.398 --> 00:29:37.433
I just don't understand.

00:29:37.468 --> 00:29:39.231
After everything we have done for you.

00:29:39.266 --> 00:29:42.358
After Roy healed you.

00:29:43.312 --> 00:29:47.658
I'm just very very disappointed Dean.

00:29:48.994 --> 00:29:51.467
You can let him go. I'm
not gonna press charges.

00:29:51.502 --> 00:29:56.656
The Lord will deal
with him as he sees fit.

00:29:58.401 --> 00:29:59.976
We catch you around here again son.

00:30:00.011 --> 00:30:02.727
Who put the fear god in you, understand?

00:30:02.762 --> 00:30:04.494
Yes, sir. Fear god.

00:30:04.529 --> 00:30:06.348
Got it.

00:30:09.400 --> 00:30:10.932
Leila.

00:30:11.621 --> 00:30:13.244
Why would you do that Dean?

00:30:13.279 --> 00:30:15.574
It could have been my only chance.

00:30:15.609 --> 00:30:17.551
He's not a healer.

00:30:17.586 --> 00:30:19.493
He healed you.

00:30:21.131 --> 00:30:23.174
I know it doesn't seem fair.

00:30:23.209 --> 00:30:27.808
And I wish I could explain. But
Roy's not the answer, I'm sorry.

00:30:29.787 --> 00:30:32.293
Goodbye Dean.

00:30:36.870 --> 00:30:40.839
I wish you luck. I really do.

00:30:40.874 --> 00:30:43.451
Same to you.

00:30:47.427 --> 00:30:50.721
You deserve it a lot more than me.

00:30:54.074 --> 00:30:56.539
Private session tonight.
No interruptions.

00:30:56.574 --> 00:30:59.004
I give you my word.
I'll heal your daughter.

00:30:59.039 --> 00:31:02.530
Thank you, reverend. God bless you.

00:31:06.640 --> 00:31:09.913
So Roy really believes.

00:31:10.452 --> 00:31:13.101
I don't think he has any
idea what his wife's doing.

00:31:13.136 --> 00:31:17.308
Well, I found this
Hidden in their library.

00:31:17.343 --> 00:31:20.604
It's ancient. Written by a
priest who went dark side.

00:31:20.639 --> 00:31:22.678
There's a binding spell in here.

00:31:22.713 --> 00:31:24.502
For trapping a reaper.

00:31:24.537 --> 00:31:26.889
Must be hell of a spell. Yeah.

00:31:26.924 --> 00:31:30.148
You got to build a black altar
with seriously dark stuff.

00:31:30.183 --> 00:31:33.637
Bones. Human blood.

00:31:33.672 --> 00:31:37.132
To cross a line like
that. That preacher's wife.

00:31:37.167 --> 00:31:41.676
Black magic, murder, evil.

00:31:41.711 --> 00:31:43.480
Desperate.

00:31:43.515 --> 00:31:46.788
Her husband was dying. She would
have done anything to save him.

00:31:46.823 --> 00:31:50.061
She was using the binding spell
to keep the reaper away from Roy.

00:31:50.096 --> 00:31:53.701
Cheating death. Literally.

00:31:53.736 --> 00:31:57.110
Yeah, but Roy's alive so why
is she still using the spell?

00:31:57.145 --> 00:32:02.651
Right. To force the reaper to help
the people she thinks are moral.

00:32:03.655 --> 00:32:07.116
Thank god save us from half the people
who think they're doing god's work.

00:32:07.151 --> 00:32:10.714
We got to break that binding spell Dean.

00:32:12.928 --> 00:32:15.325
You know Sue Ann had to
cop a cross like this.

00:32:15.360 --> 00:32:17.687
And when she dropped it
the reaper backed off.

00:32:17.722 --> 00:32:20.599
So you think we got to find
the cross or destroy the altar.

00:32:20.634 --> 00:32:22.578
Maybe both?

00:32:23.610 --> 00:32:26.025
Whatever we do. We'd
better to do it soon.

00:32:26.060 --> 00:32:29.021
Roy's healing Leila tonight.

00:32:40.866 --> 00:32:42.742
That's Leila's car.

00:32:42.777 --> 00:32:44.618
She's already here.

00:32:44.653 --> 00:32:46.405
Yeah.

00:32:47.166 --> 00:32:49.907
Dean. You know, if Roy would
have picked Leila instead of me.

00:32:49.942 --> 00:32:52.067
She'd be healed by now. Dean, don't.

00:32:52.102 --> 00:32:54.385
And if she's not healed tonight...

00:32:54.420 --> 00:32:56.813
She's gonna die in a couple of months.

00:32:56.848 --> 00:32:59.172
What's happening to her is horrible.

00:32:59.207 --> 00:33:03.518
But what are you going to do?
Let somebody else die to save her?

00:33:03.553 --> 00:33:08.183
You said it yourself
Dean. You can't play god.

00:33:22.034 --> 00:33:23.071
Gather around.

00:33:23.106 --> 00:33:25.259
Please, everyone gather around.

00:33:25.294 --> 00:33:27.412
Come in closer. Come on up.

00:33:27.447 --> 00:33:29.704
Where's Sue Ann?

00:33:30.129 --> 00:33:32.144
House.

00:33:32.956 --> 00:33:34.464
Go find Sue Ann. I'll catch up.

00:33:34.499 --> 00:33:35.981
What are you...

00:33:37.363 --> 00:33:39.013
Hey.

00:33:39.723 --> 00:33:43.099
You're gonna put that fear god in me?

00:34:26.751 --> 00:34:28.534
See him?

00:34:28.858 --> 00:34:30.692
Na.

00:34:51.661 --> 00:34:54.086
Psycho mutt.

00:35:39.433 --> 00:35:43.579
I gave your brother a life
and I can take it away.

00:35:55.132 --> 00:35:57.042
Sam, can't you see?

00:35:57.077 --> 00:35:58.917
The Lord chose me.

00:35:58.952 --> 00:36:01.687
The reward the just
and punish the wicked.

00:36:01.722 --> 00:36:04.070
And your brother is wicked.

00:36:04.105 --> 00:36:08.485
And he deserves to die just
as Leila deserves to live.

00:36:08.520 --> 00:36:11.219
That's god's will.

00:36:13.429 --> 00:36:15.948
Goodbye Sam.

00:36:20.014 --> 00:36:21.700
Mrs. Roke.

00:36:21.735 --> 00:36:23.909
You pray with me now.

00:36:23.944 --> 00:36:26.084
Pray with me friends.

00:36:55.225 --> 00:36:57.298
All right now.

00:36:58.361 --> 00:37:01.187
All right now.

00:37:26.927 --> 00:37:28.857
All right.

00:37:54.370 --> 00:37:59.587
I don't understand. I
don't feel different.

00:38:00.425 --> 00:38:01.495
My god!

00:38:01.530 --> 00:38:03.449
What have you done?

00:38:03.484 --> 00:38:05.368
He's not your god.

00:38:05.403 --> 00:38:07.407
Reverend?

00:38:07.442 --> 00:38:09.412
Sue Ann?

00:38:55.727 --> 00:38:57.444
You okay?

00:38:57.732 --> 00:38:59.801
A little bit weak.

00:38:59.836 --> 00:39:01.472
Yeah.

00:39:02.674 --> 00:39:04.534
All right, come on.

00:39:04.569 --> 00:39:06.394
We should get going.

00:39:17.740 --> 00:39:19.834
What is it?

00:39:19.869 --> 00:39:21.928
Nothing.

00:39:23.307 --> 00:39:24.585
What is it?

00:39:24.620 --> 00:39:26.550
We did the right thing here, didn't' we?

00:39:26.585 --> 00:39:28.618
Of course we did.

00:39:28.653 --> 00:39:30.975
I didn't feel like it.

00:39:32.073 --> 00:39:33.784
I got it.

00:39:37.610 --> 00:39:41.005
Leila, come on in. Hey.

00:39:41.040 --> 00:39:42.916
Hey.

00:39:43.762 --> 00:39:45.570
How did you know we were here?

00:39:45.605 --> 00:39:47.461
Sam called.

00:39:47.496 --> 00:39:51.242
He said you wanted to say goodbye.

00:39:51.409 --> 00:39:54.423
I'm gonna grab a soda.

00:39:59.143 --> 00:40:01.268
So um...

00:40:01.303 --> 00:40:04.484
Where are you going?

00:40:04.519 --> 00:40:05.690
Don't know yet.

00:40:05.725 --> 00:40:09.769
Our work kind of takes us all over so...

00:40:11.499 --> 00:40:15.863
You know, I went back to see Roy.

00:40:15.898 --> 00:40:18.527
What happened?

00:40:19.756 --> 00:40:22.068
Nothing.

00:40:22.290 --> 00:40:28.313
He laid his hand on my
forehead. But nothing happened.

00:40:28.348 --> 00:40:30.907
I'm sorry.

00:40:31.091 --> 00:40:33.670
I'm sorry it didn't work.

00:40:33.705 --> 00:40:35.642
And Sue Ann...

00:40:35.677 --> 00:40:37.342
She's dead, you know?

00:40:37.377 --> 00:40:39.292
A stroke.

00:40:39.327 --> 00:40:42.411
Yeah, I heard.

00:40:43.068 --> 00:40:46.210
Yeah, Roy's a good man.

00:40:46.383 --> 00:40:49.614
He doesn't deserve what's happened.

00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:54.845
Must be ruff...

00:40:54.880 --> 00:40:57.250
To believe in something so much.

00:40:57.285 --> 00:41:00.665
And have it disappoint you like that.

00:41:04.801 --> 00:41:08.103
You want to hear something weird?

00:41:09.304 --> 00:41:14.131
I'm okay. Really.

00:41:14.166 --> 00:41:16.525
I guess if you're gonna have faith

00:41:16.560 --> 00:41:19.703
We can't just have it
when the miracles happen.

00:41:19.738 --> 00:41:24.978
You have to have it when they don't.

00:41:29.628 --> 00:41:33.077
So what now?

00:41:35.489 --> 00:41:39.977
God works in mysterious ways.

00:41:44.107 --> 00:41:46.479
Goodbye Dean.

00:41:48.207 --> 00:41:49.923
Hey.

00:41:55.176 --> 00:42:00.269
I'm not much of a praying type but...

00:42:01.137 --> 00:42:04.611
I'm gonna pray for you.

00:42:05.769 --> 00:42:08.118
Well...

00:42:08.284 --> 00:42:11.769
There's a miracle right there.



